.official [9d84f3d13]\nv4.6.dev2.official [7864ac801]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev3 - EndeavourOS #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sun, 19 Oct 2025 19:21:18 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (nvidia; 580.95.05) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.53 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nRichTextLabel's Horizontal Alignment is broken in 4.6 dev 3, pushing the text towards the left. This is more noticable with bitmap pixel fonts at a lower resolution. Regular Labels still work as expected. Below are screenshot comparisons of the same scene between 4.6 dev 2 and dev 3, showing the bug.\n\n<img width=\"1150\" height=\"397\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f6d1a451-f53b-4d20-b398-627edf9b6001\" />\n\n<img width=\"1285\" height=\"420\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6b72438-3053-42a3-bcea-e10960dac8e5\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a RichTextLabel and set its Horizontal Alignment to either Center or Right. Both the editor option or setting it using BBCode produce the same result.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23459373/MRP.zip)\n\nOpening this project in 4.6 dev 2 will have both the RichTextLabels and Labels aligned as expected.\nOpening this project in 4.6 dev 3 will have the RichTextLabels be offset to the left compared to the Labels.\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.co